From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Reject schemas when SAX template compilation reports errors

Saxon throws IllegalStateException from getTemplates after reporting
stylesheet compilation failures. Convert only already reported schema
errors to IncorrectSchemaException; propagate unrelated state failures.

Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
--- a/mod/schematron/src/main/com/thaiopensource/validate/schematron/SchemaReaderImpl.java
+++ b/mod/schematron/src/main/com/thaiopensource/validate/schematron/SchemaReaderImpl.java
@@ -376,7 +376,16 @@
       if (ceh.getHadErrorOrFatalError())
         throw new IncorrectSchemaException();
       // Getting the templates can cause errors to be generated.
-      Templates templates = templatesHandler.getTemplates();
+      Templates templates;
+      try {
+        templates = templatesHandler.getTemplates();
+      }
+      catch (IllegalStateException e) {
+        // Saxon reports compilation errors before throwing from getTemplates().
+        if (ceh.getHadErrorOrFatalError())
+          throw new IncorrectSchemaException();
+        throw e;
+      }
       if (ceh.getHadErrorOrFatalError())
         throw new IncorrectSchemaException();
       return new SchemaImpl(templates,
